<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="idb9961aa3-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8" identifier="/us/usc/t18/s3235"><ns0:num value="3235">§ 3235.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Venue in capital cases</ns0:heading><ns0:content>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">The trial of offenses punishable with death shall be had in the county where the offense was committed, where that can be done without great inconvenience.</ns0:p>
</ns0:content><ns0:sourceCredit id="idb9961aa4-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">(<ns0:ref href="/us/act/1948-06-25/ch645">June 25, 1948, ch. 645</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/62/826">62 Stat. 826</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
<ns0:notes type="uscNote" id="idb9961aa5-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="historicalAndRevision" id="idb9961aa6-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Historical and Revision Notes</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Based on <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t28/s101">section 101 of title 28</ns0:ref>, U.S.C., 1940 ed., Judicial Code and Judiciary (<ns0:ref href="/us/act/1911-03-03/ch231/s40">Mar. 3, 1911, ch. 231, § 40</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/36/1100">36 Stat. 1100</ns0:ref>).</ns0:p>
